{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784301821,"nonce":"LHeKKYd2yv5j67l6zxQh1QYqh/M=","title":"[dogfood] log-tail spams warn every ~3s while a step Pod is PodInitializing","message":"While a step Pod is still initializing (image pull / init containers), the log tail repeatedly logs at WARN:\n\n  log tail ended with error run=... step=check error=executor error: exec error: ApiError: container \"step\" ... is waiting to start: PodInitializing: BadRequest (code 400 ...)\n\nIt retries every ~3s and floods the server log for the whole init window (can be minutes on a cold image pull). PodInitializing is an expected pre-start state, not an error — the tail should treat 'container waiting to start' as 'not ready yet, back off quietly' and only warn on genuine failures. Observed on dogfood run 68af6899 (colima). Related to the known log-dup rough edge.","files":null}]}